<article class="env-lemma" id="0DQ0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DQ0">Lemma <span data-tag="0DQ0">109.4.2</span>.</a> The morphism $\textit{PolarizedCurves} \to \mathcal{C}\! \mathit{urves}$ is smooth and surjective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Surjective. Given a field $k$ and a proper algebraic space $X$ over $k$ of dimension $\leq 1$, i.e., an object of $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{urves}$ over $k$. By Spaces over Fields, Lemma <a href="/tag/0ADD" data-tag="0ADD">72.9.3</a> the algebraic space $X$ is a scheme. Hence $X$ is a proper scheme of dimension $\leq 1$ over $k$. By Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A26" data-tag="0A26">33.43.4</a> we see that $X$ is H-projective over $\kappa $. In particular, there exists an ample invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{L}$ on $X$. Then $(X, \mathcal{L})$ is an object of $\textit{PolarizedCurves}$ over $k$ which maps to $X$. 
    <p>
      Smooth. Let $X \to S$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{urves}$, i.e., a morphism $S \to \mathcal{C}\! \mathit{urves}$. It is clear that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \textit{PolarizedCurves} \times _{\mathcal{C}\! \mathit{urves}} S \subset \mathcal{P}\! \mathit{ic}_{X/S}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is the substack of objects $(T/S, \mathcal{L}/X_ T)$ such that $\mathcal{L}$ is ample on $X_ T/T$. This is an open substack by Descent on Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0D3D" data-tag="0D3D">74.13.2</a>. Since $\mathcal{P}\! \mathit{ic}_{X/S} \to S$ is smooth by Moduli Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DPJ" data-tag="0DPJ">108.8.5</a> we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>